        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "d10d920c095de2d63a27c67e6a165fe789dbcc78",
            "parents": [
                "0e78828ce927548b4dd679e06fdaf2f294983289"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/76/78176/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                "username": "rohitpai"
            },
            "createdOn": 1739339105,
            "author": {
                "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                "username": "rohitpai"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why??  What daemon is going to implement this?  Why is it different from the \"normal\" factory reset?\n\n\"Company specific dbus interface in a public daemon\" is rarely going to fly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Nvidia platforms have additional eMMC storage and we have migrated some log functionality and flight data recorder logs. Customers need any API to clear this logs and currently this is been exposed as Redfish OEM Manager reset API. \nThe backend we are preferring to support this functionality would be in bmc code management repo (https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt). A fallback option is keep this support in meta-nvidia layer. \n\nWhat recommendation we need to follow to push an PDI to com/<org> namespace ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Customers need any API to clear this logs and currently this is been exposed as Redfish OEM Manager reset API.\n\nWhy would this be a separate clear and not part of the general BMC clearing?  I don't think we're going to allow a one-off OEM manager reset API call in bmcweb.\n\n> The backend we are preferring to support this functionality would be in bmc code management repo\n\nWe need to get to the bottom of the front-end side first.  I don't think bmcweb is going to accept an OEM interface.  I also don't think bmcweb should accept an \"if mapper contains com.nvidia interface\" code, otherwise everyone's going to want to do the same random one-offs and the whole thing is going to quickly devolve.\n\nIf all you want to do is to trigger clearing some special stuff whenever the BMC factory reset is called, you can already do this without any special code.  The BMC factory reset triggers a uboot environment variable.  You can key off this variable in the init scripts, just like the BMC reset does.  An example is this: https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/ce5037892637c70b313f10f579b3ff8f8afb5e83/meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/initrdscripts/phosphor-static-norootfs-init/21-factory-reset#L10 .  It wouldn't be hard to insert similar scripts to clear additional data like an eMMC device."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "There is difference between standard BMC factory reset which clears mainly the rw filesystems vs Nvidia OEM reset where we want to clear system events, dumps and FDR data. We dont want to combine all of this in a single BMC factory reset API because we have customer use case where they want to reset settings but not clear FDR data. Hence the need of OEM reset which clears the additional data on need basis. \n\nI let @ed@tanous.net help here with how we can integrate OEM APIs in bmcweb as we definitely have use case for this. We have MRs in pipeline which allows registration of OEM handles per vendor. https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/77056"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "@rohitpai77@gmail.com please add some of these details to the commit message. Also, do we need to think of this in terms \"where to perform reset\" vs the \"what - FDR/events/etc.\"? That is, if the existing interface clears only the SPI data flash, where do the other Nvidia things sit - emmc? somewhere else? Are those area generic enough to modify/extend the existing interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "@deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com updated the commit message based on your suggestion PTAL."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
