            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not true.  We have `xyz.openbmc_project.Common.FactoryReset` and there are already multiple paths understood by bmcweb.\n\n```\n$ rg \"Common.FactoryReset\"                                                   \nredfish-core/lib/bios.hpp\n116:        \"xyz.openbmc_project.Common.FactoryReset\", \"Reset\");\n\nredfish-core/lib/managers.hpp\n283:                \"xyz.openbmc_project.Common.FactoryReset\", \"Reset\");\n```\n\nWe should do two things here, rather than define a whole new interface:\n\n1. Document the existing paths in Common.FactoryReset for BMC and BIOS reset.  (See the \"paths:\" section in the interface file.)\n\n2. Add a new path for your additional use case.  Hopefully this can be worded in a way that is not specific to Nvidia (since it seems like you're generically targeting additional debug data).  I would suggest inquiring with the phosphor-debug-collector maintainers for an appropriate word to describe your collection."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the above suggestions. \n\nCurrently we want to use this API for erasing all contents in our additional storage which is dumps, logs. But we could add more things to the same partition. \nIf we consider the existing Factory Reset, its not tied up any specific type of data or backend service. We would like create something generic not tie it up with debug collector or phosphor logs alone. \n\nI can definitely consider if there is a way to make this generic. \nFor erasing dumps alone we have RF APIs. But we would like ease multiple types of data under single API. Would like to consider the same design approach as current factory reset which set the env variable and erase of the partition happens at startup. \n\nPlease let me know if you have further thought on how to make this generic."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is the redfish API you intend to use for this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "```/redfish/v1/Managers/{managerid}/Actions/Oem/NvidiaManager.ResetToDefaults ```\nthis is the other reason I thought we can create OEM PDI for this action"
                },
